battlefield one is finally here in all  of its mud and bloody glory for all to  take in  we finally gotten our hands on a  finished product and to kick things off  here our top six newest features added  to battlefield one we've seen Zeppelin's  two heavily armoured trains in the past  but now the third behemoth is here the  dreadnought this battleship is ready to  sink your dreams of victory with one of  its four heavy cannons that are powerful  enough to level capture points on sight  followed by also having anti-infantry  guns mounted on its side it's perfect to  support infantry pushing up the enemy  beachhead it took all of my grenades a  few heavy cannon shells from my base  defenses a few warplanes to slow this  ship down even then it will leave its  mark on the field and in your soldiers  Minds even as it sinks into the sea  speaking of boats returning from bf4 our  attack boats to combat both dreadknots  and land-based fortresses these fast and  agile boats are excellent for covering  long distances allowing yourself to  flank your enemies also when driving  you'll have two torpedoes I can do heavy  damage to other boats and/or ships in  your sights  sporting heavy machine guns on both  sides and in front of your boat for your  passengers this thing is ready to take  on the high seas for any mission you see  fit some new equipment has returned from  the days of bf4 such as the motor for  the support class with three different  types of ammunition and a surprising  high splash damage upon hitting its  target these motors are the go-to  weapons for launching a full frontal  assault on well defended enemy targets  able to select your target area on the  mini-map made this super useful in the  urban map of arms where enemy soldiers  hided in bombed-out houses all over the  place this is the go-to weapon to use to  take out pesky enemies hiding in those  houses  a new century kid has made its way in  the form of a to magazine SMG that can  drop your foes faster than you can blink  just like it's heavy armored cousins the  flamethrower and the heavy machine gun  this kit gives you full protection and  knights in shining armor look along with  a weapon that is just too powerful to be  true just 5 rounds from its 25 round  magazine can drop any player regardless  of the character he plays this kind of  firepower helped lead me to a 69 kill 2  to death ratio and just one round let's  just say my opponents weren't too happy  about getting killed so quickly but hey  it's war and it sucks for them  the maps in battlefield ones final build  offer a ton of variety from fighting in  the snowy mountains in Italy to the lush  full force of the Argonne to the  sunsetting ocean coasts of Saudi Arabia  every map has its own unique beauty that  we haven't seen since Bad Company 2 the  same can also be said about the detail  and destruction each map has fortresses  turned inside out from bombings villages  torn to pieces by tank fire and mountain  tops covered an enemy shell fire all  equals to a surreal environment settings  that will pull you into the conflict and  won't let you go not that you would want  to of course some changes have been made  since the beta the horse for example no  longer has the wide range to hit and  kill your opponents so if you relied  heavily on running people over you might  be up for a surprise another thing too  is the assault class still carries the  majority of the explosives but now the  medic and support classes can do more  damage to vehicles which no longer  leaves a job to just one character a new  mode titled operations which is a cross  between Rush and conquest has players  battle it out to hold capture points and  fix locations on each section of the map  with attacking and defending teams with  the behemoths making a more important  role to play it's a mode that feels like  something we as battlefield vets have  been waiting for for a long time little  changes to audio and environment weather  also plays a part in the player to  player needs on a whole new level for so  long I wanted to relive those awesome  close call battles and fully destroyed  maps back in back company to battlefield  3 4 and hard lines failed to give me  that rush I missed but battlefield 1  feels like the game to keep me and my  friends busy for months to come if  you're a vet of the series but are on  the fence about jumping into this one  take it from me you will find the same  adrenaline rush shootout mayhem and  vehicle warfare the series has been  missing is there anything you want to  see or hope for in the months to come to  support battlefield one feel free to  leave your comments below and until next  time we'll see you on the battlefield  and keep it here on gamespot for all  your gaming needs  [Music]
 

